- op: update  # 7356
  at: '2026-06-30T12:38:07Z'  # 7356
  by: agent  # 7356
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7356
  clock: 5  # 7356
  nonce: '7356'  # 7356
  set:  # 7356
    status: needs_human_review  # 7356
    priority: 3  # 7356
    title: "framework_dispatch meta-key at recurrence-promotion threshold — promote to Edge.framework? (ADR-0028 OQ2)"  # 7356
    description: "RE-SCOPED 2026-06-30 (wave3 plan §A row 9; tracker hygiene, no code).\n\nORIGINAL premise (RESOLVED): the edge.meta.framework_dispatch axis mixed\nframework names (fastapi, starlette, django_channels) with mechanism/pattern\ncategories (registry_dispatch 89%, native_websocket, rust_trait_dispatch) and\npackaging nouns (npm_package, html_script_src) — two/three axes in one field.\n\nRESOLVED BY audit-findings 0014 (Cluster 28C, docs/audits/0014-evidence-type-cluster-c-framework-dispatch.md):\nthe meta-key partition splits the cluster — 56 framework-named rows fold to\nmeta[\"framework_dispatch\"]=<framework_name>; 9 pattern/mechanism rows\n(registry_dispatch, naming/URL/regex matches, etc.) fold to\nmeta[\"detection_pattern\"]=<pattern_name>. After the fold, framework_dispatch\nholds framework names only; the mechanism leak is gone. Shipped via Wave 5 of\nWI-runod (Codeberg #3572 + selfh #162-#166); audit 0014 status: All RESOLVED.\n\nRE-SCOPED CONCERN (this item now tracks): ADR-0028 Open Question 2 — the\nrecurrence-promotion threshold. Post-fold, meta[\"framework_dispatch\"] carries\n~30 distinct framework-name values across ~30 producer modules, which is AT the\nADR-0024 §\"Fold-residue discipline\" rule-3 threshold (>=30 distinct values\nacross >=30 producers). Open decision: should framework_dispatch promote from\nan Edge.meta key to a dedicated Edge.framework: str | None field? Gated on\npost-migration steady-state emission-count confirmation (needs a diverse-corpus\nbakeoff, not self-analysis — hypergumbo's own deps exercise only a few of the\n~30 frameworks, so a self-corpus count under-counts). If the threshold is\nconfirmed tripped, the promotion is a follow-on ADR (or an ADR-0028 §6\namendment) adding the field with its ADR-0024 axis scaffolding — a human\narchitectural call, hence needs_human_review."  # 7356
  add:  # 7356
    tags: [promotion_threshold]  # 7356
- op: discuss  # 4e19
